{{!--
  The desktop entry the .deb, the .rpm and the AppImage install (the AUR and
  COPR packages repackage the first two). It is Tauri's own template with two
  changes:

  - `Exec` takes `%F`. Without a field code the file manager starts WaveFlow
    with no file at all, so "Open with WaveFlow" opened an empty window.
    `%F` hands over local paths, mounting a remote file through GIO first;
    `launch_args` reads them, and a second launch passes them on to the
    running window.
  - `MimeType` lists the formats WaveFlow plays, with the legacy aliases
    (`audio/x-flac`, ...) older shared-mime-info databases still report.
    It is written here rather than taken from `bundle.fileAssociations`:
    those are declared for macOS only (tauri.macos.conf.json), since in the
    base config Windows would make them every format's default, and the
    `--config` overlay scripts/tauri.mjs passes undoes a platform file's
    attempt to remove them.

  Keep the formats in step with tauri.macos.conf.json, the Windows
  `open-with` hooks and the Flatpak desktop entry.
--~}}
[Desktop Entry]
Categories={{categories}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %F
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
MimeType=audio/mpeg;audio/flac;audio/x-flac;audio/wav;audio/x-wav;audio/aiff;audio/x-aiff;audio/ogg;audio/x-vorbis+ogg;audio/opus;audio/x-opus+ogg;audio/mp4;audio/x-m4a;audio/aac;audio/x-dsf;audio/x-dff;
